NV_PK(13,{"this bixi is not at chihkan tower it is at baoan temple in nanchang tainan legend says ten stone turtles came with the steles in 1788 and one fell into the sea while it was being unloaded in 1911 it was dug up from a fish pond today people worship it as the lady of the white lotus":"","long ago pairs of stone animals guarded the tombs of important officials legend says this stone horse once guarded koxinga's tomb in 1786 a militia leader who died in the lin shuangwen uprising was buried there the horses did not want to guard him so they ran wild in the fields at night angry villagers broke their legs its partner horse stands behind a temple in yongkang":"","the orange plaque says sea god temple old chinese signs are read from right to left the sea god temple and wenchang pavilion were both built on the old dutch base in the qing dynasty look up at the painted beams and the lantern":"","this old map was drawn by the spanish in manila in 1626 it shows the dutch harbor in taiwan a fort on a sandbar and a big inner sea where ships sailed long ago before the taijiang sea filled up with mud the waves came right up to chihkan tower":"","this model shows what fort provintia may have looked like when the dutch built it with white houses red roofs and little corner towers the dutch began building it in 1653":"","this glass case shows old pieces of the building the carved wooden beam was taken out during a repair the small round piece is a tile end from the edge of a qing style roof behind them the green window bars look like bamboo":"","this doorway is shaped like a vase in chinese the word for vase sounds like the word for peace so the door wishes everyone a safe and peaceful life":"","above the vase shaped door of the sea god temple a white rabbit rests on a big green banana leaf it is made of clay in chinese stories a jade rabbit lives on the moon":"","legend says one bixi fell into the sea while it was being unloaded in 1911 it was dug up and today it is worshipped at baoan temple in nanchang":"","the tenth bixi spent more than 120 years underwater and became a goddess":""});